{"id":"G1437","lemma":"ἐάν","transliteration":"ean","sayIt":"ean","language":"Greek","partOfSpeech":"","gloss":"if","meaning":"ἐάν, contr. fr. εἰ ἄν,\nconditional particle,\nrepresenting something as \"under certain circumstances actual or liable to happen,\" but not so definitely expected as in the case of εἰ with ind. (Bl., §65, 4; cf. Jhn.13:17, 1Co.7:36), if haply, if;\n1. with subjc. (cl.);\n(a) pres.: Mat.6:22, Luk.10:6, Jhn.7:17, Rom.2:25, 26 al.;\n{ (b) aor. (= Lat. fut. pf.): Mat.4:9 16:26 (cf. ptcp. in Luk.9:25; M, Pr., 230), Mrk.3:24, Luk.14:34, Jhn.5:43, Rom.7:2, al.; = cl. εἰ, with opt., Jhn.9:22 11:57, Act.9:2; as Heb. אִם = ὅταν, Jhn.12:32 14:3, I Jhn.2:28 3:2, Heb.3:7\" (LXX) .\n2. C. indic, (as in late writers, fr. Arist. on; see WH, App., 171; VD, MGr. 2, App., §77; Deiss., BS, 201f., LAE, 155, 254; M, Pr., 168, 187; Bl., §65, 4);\n(a) fut.: Mat.18:19 T, Luk.19:40, Act.7:7;\n(b) pres.: 1Th.3:8 (see Milligan, in l.).\n3. With other particles: ἐ. καί (Bl., §65, 6), Gal.6:1; ἐ. μή (M, Pr., 185, 187; Bl., l.with), with subjc. pres., Mat.10:13, 1Co.8:8, Jas.2:17, 1Jn.3:21; aor., Mat.6:15, Mrk.3:27, Jhn.3:3, Rom.10:15, Gal.1:8 2:16 (see Lft., Ellic., in ll.); ἐ. τε . . . ἐ. τε, [in LXX for אִם . . . אִם, Est.19:13, al.,] Rom.14:8.\n4. = cl. ἄν (which see) after relat. pronouns and adverbs (Tdf., Pr., 96; WH, App., 173; M, Pr., 42f.; Bl., §26, 4; Mayser, 152f.; Deiss., BS, 202ff.): ὃς ἐ., Mat.5:19, Mrk.6:22, 23 Luk.17:32, 1Co.6:18, al.; ὅπου ἐ., Mat.8:19; ὁσάκις ἐ., Rev.11:6; οὗ ἐ., 1Co.16:6; καθὸ ἐ., 2Co.8:12; ὅστις ἐ., Gal.5:10.\n(AS)","glosses":["if","unless","whatever","when","whoever","wherever"],"count":310,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"mat-4","v":9,"renderings":{"bsb":"if","kjv":"if"}},{"chapterId":"mat-5","v":13,"renderings":{"bsb":"if","kjv":"if"}},{"chapterId":"mat-5","v":19,"renderings":{"bsb":"So then","kjv":"Whosoever"}},{"chapterId":"mat-5","v":20,"renderings":{"bsb":"unless"}},{"chapterId":"mat-5","v":23,"renderings":{"bsb":"if","kjv":"if"}}